ReadyStack 0005: libssl3 3.0.22-1~deb12u2 (bookworm-security) over the distroless base, in all five images.

gcr.io/distroless/base-debian12 (WORKSPACE go_image_base, and its newest latest-amd64 too) carries libssl3
3.0.20-1~deb12u2: CVE-2026-75803 (critical), CVE-2026-63072, CVE-2026-63076, CVE-2026-54874 (high; fixed in
3.0.22-1~deb12u1) and CVE-2026-84782 (high; fixed in 3.0.22-1~deb12u2). //distroless-overrides:libssl3_x86_64 is the
.deb from a fixed snapshot.debian.org URL (sha256 cb4784740daa9b3b0eaea2b444bbefa686794afbbf3d678d238c1fd9875f2efd), laid out the way distroless builds its own
layers: data.tar plus var/lib/dpkg/status.d/libssl3 (+ .md5sums), so every scanner reads the installed version.
Remove when gcr.io/distroless/base-debian12 ships libssl3 >= 3.0.22-1~deb12u2 (then bump go_image_base instead,
hack/bump-distroless.sh).

